    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The app config-app in namespace scenario-test is failing to start. Investigate whether ConfigMap or Secret data is the cause."
      }
    ],
    "final_text": "INVESTIGATION_PLAN:\n1. Describe the failing pod `config-app-78f497df98-vk78v` in the `scenario-test` namespace to confirm the exact missing ConfigMap or Secret name.\n2. Check if the referenced ConfigMap or Secret exists in the `scenario-test` namespace.\n\nProceeding with tool calls.### Findings:\n1. The pod `config-app-78f497df98-vk78v` in the `scenario-test` namespace is failing with the reason `CreateContainerConfigError`.\n2. The pod references a ConfigMap named `nonexistent-config` as an environment variable source, but this ConfigMap does not exist in the `scenario-test` namespace.\n3. The only ConfigMap present in the namespace is `kube-root-ca.crt`, which is unrelated to the pod's requirements.\n\n### Root Cause:\nThe pod is configured to use a ConfigMap named `nonexistent-config`, which is missing in the `scenario-test` namespace.\n\n### Suggested Fix:\n1. Create the missing ConfigMap `nonexistent-config` in the `scenario-test` namespace with the required data.\n   Example command:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl create configmap nonexistent-config --from-literal=key=value -n scenario-test\n   ```\n2. Alternatively, update the pod specification to reference an existing ConfigMap or remove the dependency if it's not required.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with creating the ConfigMap or provide further assistance?",
